stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> TerminalRunning: A tool starts a terminal

    TerminalRunning --> ExitStarted: You quit fx
    ExitStarted --> TreeNoted: fx writes down the terminal's processes
    TreeNoted --> TreeNoted: The shell starts a child in its own group
    TreeNoted --> ShellHungUp: fx hangs up the shell, which ends, and keeps the launcher's process entry
    ShellHungUp --> SessionEmpty: fx ends every process of the launcher's session, then collects the entry
    SessionEmpty --> FxGone: fx exits after a bounded wait

    ShellHungUp --> ChildHoldsPty: Planted record_once, only the noted processes die
    ShellHungUp --> ChildHoldsPty: Planted early_reap, fx collected the launcher's entry too soon, so nothing names the session
    ChildHoldsPty --> FxGoneHeld: fx exits after the wait
    ShellHungUp --> LauncherWaits: Planted launcher_wait, the launcher waits for a release that cannot come
    LauncherWaits --> FxGoneHeld: fx exits after the wait

    TerminalRunning --> Orphaned: fx crashes
    Orphaned --> TerminalGone: The kernel hangs up the PTY
    Orphaned --> DaemonLives: A program that ignores the hangup stays

    FxGone --> [*]
    FxGoneHeld --> [*]
    TerminalGone --> [*]
    DaemonLives --> [*]

    note right of FxGoneHeld
        Breaks NoHolderAfterCleanExit: after a normal exit something still
        holds the PTY, which keeps its backend from draining.
        Shortest paths: launcher_wait takes 7 steps, Start, OpenBegin,
        BeginExit, ExitRecord, ExitHangup, ExitKill, FinishExit. record_once
        adds ForkLate after ExitRecord, and early_reap adds ReapLauncher after
        ExitHangup.
    end note

    note right of SessionEmpty
        Left out: a program that moved to its own session with setsid, which
        survives the exit by design and, when it keeps the PTY open, is why the
        wait is bounded; a host daemon that keeps terminals past a clean exit
        (daemon_survives, which breaks OrphansOnlyAfterCrash); a start that
        has not returned (list_in_flight, end_at_return); reconcile and resume
        (profile_wide_recover, reattach); a terminal that ends by itself; and a
        second fx process.
    end note
